<title>FRANCE: France Telecom says Sprint report &quot;wrong&quot;.</title>
<headline>France Telecom says Sprint report &quot;wrong&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>France Telecom on Monday described as &quot;wrong&quot; a German magazine report which said the French state telecoms operator and German Deutsche Telekom AG wanted to take a majority in U.S. telephone company Sprint, a partner in their global alliance.</p>
<p>&quot;It's wrong,&quot; a France Telecom spokesman said in reply to a query from Reuters on the report in Focus magazine.</p>
<p>France Telecom and Deutsche Telekom each have 10 percent of Sprint.</p>
</text>
